From 243d2588fea991db4add0d576764dc1f0352572d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koudai Aono <koxudaxi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:35:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] mellum: exact q8 metal graph and rewind

The Q8_0 Metal graph: q/k norm and RoPE with YaRN on the full layers only,
ring commit and sliding-window attention, ungated full attention on the
upstream qwen4 decode kernels, MoE with top-8 of 64 routed experts and no
shared expert, the layer loop and logits, and the DS4_MELLUM_TRACE driver.

Rewind: one token back keeps both caches; at the last sync's end the
frontier's rings and logits are restored; anywhere else the graph resets and
the kept tokens are replayed. The exact rows kernel makes a replay equal the
decode steps it replaces.

Asserted by tests/test_mellum_kernels.c (509 checks), the trace driver's
untraced-versus-fully-traced logit equality, and ds4_test --mellum-rewind at
500/1, 1100/1, 1100/3 and the 1100/40 frontier case: zero differing logit
words, and the stale-frontier rewind resets. On the real Q8_0 GGUF, 64 greedy
token ids match the fork's CLI at d2d9338.

Upstream: not offered, fork only
Retire-when: upstream runs an exact Mellum 2.1 Metal graph
